      "content": "the problem is if we even mention a \"clerical error\" or say we'll provide an \"updated ETA,\" the client is gonna start asking questions and realize we're behind. if they catch on that we aren't 100% on track, they'll push for the penalty immediately.\n\nis there a way to write this so we don't mention the error at all? can we just frame it as \"processing is underway\" or something that implies they're already moving through customs without actually saying they're stuck?",
